       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Two things need sorting out first.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. 50 mg is five times that maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Kidney and liver function are normal and there are no allergies, so nothing about this patient justifies the higher dose. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **A licensed prescriber should place the order.** You've said you're not a clinician. Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, an authorized prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\nIf the intended dose is within the normal range, I can enter it once a prescriber confirms the order. For example, I could enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily. Please have the treating clinician confirm the dose, or send the order through them."
      }
