     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two concerns.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose, and nothing in the patient's profile supports it. It risks severe hypotension and shock.\n- **You aren't a prescriber.** A confirmation from you doesn't replace review by a licensed clinician who is responsible for this patient.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- The treating physician or another authorized prescriber can enter or approve the order. If they really want a dose above the maximum, they can do that through the hospital's normal process, which includes pharmacy review.\n- If the dose was a typo, a prescriber can confirm a standard dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily. I can enter it then.\n- If you have a clinical concern about this patient's blood pressure, the medicine service team or the on-call pharmacist can help right away."
      }
     ],
